.TH MU2E-KRB-CRON.PY 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-controlroom t01.00.00" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
mu2e\-krb\-cron.py \- keytab\-based Kerberos ticket keeper meant to run from cron (deprecated)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B python3 mu2e\-krb\-cron.py
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-v | \-\-verbose ]
.RB [ \-s | \-\-silent ]
.RB [ \-n | \-\-dry\-run ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Deprecated.
Ticket minting, renewal and cache management are provided by
.B mu2edaq\-kerberos
.RB ( get\-kerberos\-ticket (1),
.BR ticket\-manager (1),
.BR mu2edaq\-krb (1)),
which keeps keytabs in Vault instead of on disk.
That package has no unattended, cron\-style equivalent of this script;
see
.B BUGS
before using this one.
.PP
Each run looks only at the principal of the
.I default
credential cache (python\-krb5
.BR cc_default )
and does exactly one of:
.TP
.B no ticket
.B kinit
from keytab for every configured principal, in order.
.TP
.B principal not in the configured list
.BR kdestroy ,
then
.B kinit
from keytab for every configured principal.
.TP
.B allowed principal, at least renew_threshold_hours left
nothing.
.TP
.B less left, renew\-until more than renew_till_threshold_hours away
.BR "kinit \-R" .
.TP
.B less left, renew\-until closer (or unknown)
a fresh
.B kinit
from that principal's keytab.
.PP
Every path then runs
.B kswitch \-p
with the principal that
.B user_principals
maps the current OS user to, if any.
Keytab
.B kinit
uses
.B \-f \-A \-k \-t
on macOS and
.B \-5 \-F \-A \-k \-t
elsewhere.
Expiry and renew\-until are parsed from plain
.B klist
output (MIT and Heimdal date formats).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " FILE"
YAML file replacing the embedded
.B DEFAULT_CONFIG
(script lines 49\-83) entirely; missing
.B settings
keys default.
The script's own comment says production runs should use no arguments.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
DEBUG logging; wins over
.BR \-\-silent .
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-silent
WARNING and above only.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
log the
.BR kinit ,
.BR kdestroy ,
.B kswitch
commands instead of running them.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.EX
settings:
  renew_threshold_hours: 2
  renew_till_threshold_hours: 24
  log_file: /var/log/krb\-cron.log      # optional, appended
principals:                             # required, at least one
  \- name: "mu2edaq/mu2edaq/mu2e.fnal.gov@FNAL.GOV"
    keytab: "/path/to/mu2edaq.keytab"
user_principals:                        # optional: OS user \-> principal
  mu2edaq: "mu2edaq/mu2edaq/mu2e.fnal.gov@FNAL.GOV"
.EE
.PP
The embedded configuration lists six service principals with keytabs
under
.I /Users/anorman/Kerberos_Keytabs/Mu2e/
and maps the OS user
.B anorman
to
.BR anorman@FNAL.GOV ,
which is not one of the six.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /Users/anorman/Kerberos_Keytabs/Mu2e/*.keytab
keytabs named by the embedded configuration; not checked for existence or
permissions before use.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B KRB5CCNAME
honoured indirectly: it selects the default cache that python\-krb5,
.BR klist ,
.B kinit
and
.B kdestroy
act on.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on every path that reaches a decision, including when
.BR kinit ,
.B kdestroy
or
.B kswitch
fails (failures are only logged);
1 for a missing or invalid configuration, no principals, or a
python\-krb5 context failure; 2 for a command\-line error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
python3 mu2e\-krb\-cron.py \-\-dry\-run \-\-verbose
*/30 * * * * /usr/bin/python3 /path/to/mu2e\-krb\-cron.py \-\-silent
.EE
.SH BUGS
A personal ticket in the default cache is destroyed: any principal outside
.B principals
triggers
.BR kdestroy ,
including the
.B anorman@FNAL.GOV
that
.B user_principals
asks to make default.
.PP
Only the default cache is maintained.
After the first run the other configured principals' tickets are never
renewed and lapse at the end of their lifetime.
.PP
Heimdal's
.B klist
(macOS) prints no "renew until" line, so renew\-until is unknown and every
renewal becomes a fresh keytab
.BR kinit .
.PP
With a non\-collection cache type (plain
.BR FILE: ),
each keytab
.B kinit
overwrites the previous one and only the last principal survives.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR get\-kerberos\-ticket (1),
.BR ticket\-manager (1),
.BR mu2edaq\-krb (1),
.BR ticket\-manage.py (1),
.BR kinit (1),
.BR kswitch (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Andrew Norman, Mu2e DAQ group, Fermilab.
